---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";

const effective = "May 24, 2026";
const updated = "May 28, 2026";

const subprocessors = [
  ["Supabase", "Database hosting (PostgreSQL)", "Stores your account, dogs, walks, messages, and so on"],
  ["Cloudflare", "Image hosting (Cloudflare Images), serverless functions (Workers)", "Hosts dog photos, runs AI captioning and transcription"],
  ["Replicate", "AI model hosting", "Runs the models that caption photos and extract events from walk-report audio"],
  ["Stripe", "Payment processing (Stripe Connect)", "Processes all payments; stores card data per PCI-DSS"],
  ["Render", "Backend hosting", "Runs the Sniffr API"],
  ["Apple Push Notification service (APNs)", "iOS push delivery", "Delivers notifications to iPhone users"],
  ["Firebase Cloud Messaging (FCM)", "Android push delivery", "Delivers notifications to Android users"],
  ["Web Push providers", "Browser push delivery (Chrome, Firefox, Safari)", "Delivers notifications to web users"],
];
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy — Sniffr"
  description="How Sniffr handles your data — plain language, no dark patterns. What we collect, why, and the control you have over it."
>
  <article class="px-6 py-20 md:py-28">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
      <header>
        <p class="text-sm uppercase tracking-widest text-[var(--color-accent)] font-semibold">
          Legal
        </p>
        <h1 class="font-display text-5xl md:text-7xl font-semibold tracking-tight mt-3 text-balance">
          Privacy Policy
        </h1>
        <p class="mt-6 text-sm text-[var(--color-muted)]">
          Effective {effective} &middot; Last updated {updated}
        </p>
        <p class="mt-8 text-lg md:text-xl text-[var(--color-muted)] leading-relaxed">
          This policy explains what information Sniffr collects when you use the Sniffr
          app or website, why, and what control you have over it. It applies to the Sniffr
          mobile app (Android and iOS), the web app at app.sniffrpack.com, and this
          marketing site (collectively, &ldquo;Sniffr&rdquo;). Sniffr is operated by
          Papyrus Labs, based in Maplewood, New Jersey, United States.
        </p>
      </header>

      <!-- How Sniffr works -->
      <section class="mt-16">
        <h2 class="font-display text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight">
          A note on how Sniffr works
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-[var(--color-muted)] leading-relaxed">
          Sniffr is a platform that dog-walking businesses use to run their operations.
          When you use the app, you&rsquo;re using software that is run by your dog
          walker&rsquo;s business on top of Sniffr. That means two parties handle your data:
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-6 space-y-3 text-lg leading-relaxed">
          <li class="flex gap-3">
            <span class="text-[var(--color-accent)] font-semibold">&middot;</span>
            <span><strong>Your dog walker&rsquo;s business</strong> (your &ldquo;tenant&rdquo; &mdash; for example, Hamilton Bark) decides what data to collect, how to use it, and how long to keep it. They are the data controller.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex gap-3">
            <span class="text-[var(--color-accent)] font-semibold">&middot;</span>
            <span><strong>Sniffr</strong> (Papyrus Labs) provides the platform that stores and processes the data on their behalf. We are the data processor.</span>
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-6 text-lg text-[var(--color-muted)] leading-relaxed">
          If you have questions about your data &mdash; what&rsquo;s stored, how to delete
          it, how it&rsquo;s used &mdash; your first stop should be your dog walker&rsquo;s
          business. We help them respond to those requests but we don&rsquo;t make those
          decisions independently. This marketing site is the one exception: here, Sniffr
          is the controller and only collects what&rsquo;s described in the &ldquo;This
          site&rdquo; section below.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- What we collect -->
      <section class="mt-16">
        <h2 class="font-display text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight">
          What we collect
        </h2>

        <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold mt-8">Account information</h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-lg text-[var(--color-muted)] leading-relaxed">
          When you sign up (as a dog owner, walker, or business admin): name, email
          address, phone number (optional), password (stored hashed &mdash; we never see
          your actual password), and an optional profile photo.
        </p>

        <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold mt-8">Address and home-access information</h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-lg text-[var(--color-muted)] leading-relaxed">
          For dog owners, so walkers can actually do walks: home address, and any key
          location notes, lockbox codes, parking notes, or building access codes you give
          your walker. This is sensitive. It&rsquo;s stored encrypted at rest, visible only
          to your dog walker&rsquo;s business and the walkers they assign to you, and never
          shared outside that business.
        </p>

        <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold mt-8">Emergency contact</h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-lg text-[var(--color-muted)] leading-relaxed">
          Optional but encouraged: emergency contact name, phone, and relationship &mdash;
          so we can reach someone if there&rsquo;s an incident during a walk.
        </p>

        <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold mt-8">Dog information</h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-lg text-[var(--color-muted)] leading-relaxed">
          Name, breed, age, weight, color, behavioral notes; veterinarian contact
          (optional); medical notes, allergies, medications (optional); and dog photos you
          or your walker upload.
        </p>

        <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold mt-8">Service information</h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-lg text-[var(--color-muted)] leading-relaxed">
          Walks scheduled and completed, recurring &ldquo;windows&rdquo; you set up, walk
          reports, photos taken during walks, and messages exchanged between you, your
          walker, and your dog walker&rsquo;s business.
        </p>

        <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold mt-8">Audio recordings (walkers only)</h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-lg text-[var(--color-muted)] leading-relaxed">
          When walkers dictate a walk report, the audio is recorded, transmitted securely
          to our transcription service, converted to text, and then the audio is discarded.
          We retain only the text transcript. We do not store the audio file beyond the
          transcription step.
        </p>

        <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold mt-8">Camera and microphone</h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-lg text-[var(--color-muted)] leading-relaxed">
          The mobile app uses your camera (to photograph dogs and walk activity) and
          microphone (for walk-report dictation). Access is granted by you at the OS level
          when first requested; you can revoke it anytime in your device settings.
        </p>

        <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold mt-8">Payment information</h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-lg text-[var(--color-muted)] leading-relaxed">
          We use Stripe (Stripe Connect) to process payments. Sniffr never sees, stores, or
          transmits your card number, CVV, or bank credentials &mdash; those go directly
          from your device to Stripe. We store only transaction metadata (amount, date,
          what it was for) and a Stripe token that lets your dog walker&rsquo;s business
          reconcile payments.
        </p>

        <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold mt-8">Device and app information</h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-lg text-[var(--color-muted)] leading-relaxed">
          Your device&rsquo;s push-notification token (an opaque identifier from Apple,
          Google, or your browser) so we can notify you about walks and messages; app and
          OS version for diagnostics; and basic crash reports if the app crashes (stack
          traces and device model, no personal screen content).
        </p>

        <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold mt-8">What we do <em>not</em> collect</h3>
        <ul class="mt-3 space-y-2 text-lg leading-relaxed text-[var(--color-muted)]">
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-[var(--color-accent)]">&middot;</span> We do not track your live location.</li>
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-[var(--color-accent)]">&middot;</span> We do not read your contacts, calendar, SMS, or call history.</li>
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-[var(--color-accent)]">&middot;</span> We do not use third-party advertising trackers or sell your data.</li>
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-[var(--color-accent)]">&middot;</span> We do not use profile-building analytics SDKs (no Facebook SDK, no Google Analytics).</li>
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-[var(--color-accent)]">&middot;</span> We do not collect photos from your camera roll unless you explicitly pick one to upload.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- How we use it -->
      <section class="mt-16">
        <h2 class="font-display text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight">
          How we use this information
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-[var(--color-muted)] leading-relaxed">
          To provide the service you signed up for (scheduling, reports, payments,
          messaging), authenticate you, notify you about your dog&rsquo;s walks and
          messages, generate walk reports (including automated transcription and
          AI-generated photo captions), diagnose bugs, and improve the platform in
          aggregated, anonymized form. We do not use your personal information to train AI
          models &mdash; per-walk AI processing is one-shot, and inputs are not retained by
          the AI provider for training.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Sharing -->
      <section class="mt-16">
        <h2 class="font-display text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight">
          How we share information
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-[var(--color-muted)] leading-relaxed">
          Sniffr uses a small set of third-party services to operate &mdash; sub-processors
          that handle data on our behalf under contracts requiring them to protect it:
        </p>
        <div class="mt-6 overflow-x-auto">
          <table class="w-full border-collapse text-base">
            <thead>
              <tr class="border-b border-[var(--color-rule)] text-left">
                <th class="py-2 pr-4 font-semibold">Service</th>
                <th class="py-2 pr-4 font-semibold">What they handle</th>
                <th class="py-2 font-semibold">Why</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              {subprocessors.map(([service, what, why]) => (
                <tr class="border-b border-[var(--color-rule)] align-top">
                  <td class="py-2 pr-4 font-medium">{service}</td>
                  <td class="py-2 pr-4 text-[var(--color-muted)]">{what}</td>
                  <td class="py-2 text-[var(--color-muted)]">{why}</td>
                </tr>
              ))}
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-6 text-lg text-[var(--color-muted)] leading-relaxed">
          Beyond those, data goes only to your dog walker&rsquo;s business (the controller
          of your data), to you (you can view your own data in the app), and to law
          enforcement if legally required (we&rsquo;ll tell you unless prohibited). We do
          not sell data or share it with advertisers, data brokers, or marketing partners.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Retention -->
      <section class="mt-16">
        <h2 class="font-display text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight">
          How long we keep data
        </h2>
        <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-lg leading-relaxed text-[var(--color-muted)]">
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-[var(--color-accent)]">&middot;</span> Active accounts: kept while you have an active account with your dog walker&rsquo;s business.</li>
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-[var(--color-accent)]">&middot;</span> Inactive accounts: when your business leaves Sniffr, they take their customer data with them; deleted accounts are removed within 30 days.</li>
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-[var(--color-accent)]">&middot;</span> Walk audio: discarded as soon as it&rsquo;s transcribed (typically seconds).</li>
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-[var(--color-accent)]">&middot;</span> Photos: kept while your account is active; deleted with your account.</li>
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-[var(--color-accent)]">&middot;</span> Payment records: retained 7 years for financial recordkeeping.</li>
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-[var(--color-accent)]">&middot;</span> Backups: rolling 90-day; deleted data is purged from backups within 90 days.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- Rights -->
      <section class="mt-16">
        <h2 class="font-display text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight">
          Your rights
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-[var(--color-muted)] leading-relaxed">
          You can, at any time: view your account, dogs, walks, photos, and messages in the
          app; edit your contact info, address, and dog details; delete photos and messages
          directly; delete your account (contact your dog walker&rsquo;s business or email
          us &mdash; complete within 30 days, except payment records as noted); and export
          your data (email us for a machine-readable copy within 30 days). If you live in a
          jurisdiction with specific privacy rights (California CCPA/CPRA, EU/UK GDPR,
          Canada PIPEDA, etc.), those rights apply and we will honor them.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Children / Security -->
      <section class="mt-16">
        <h2 class="font-display text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight">
          Children &amp; security
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-[var(--color-muted)] leading-relaxed">
          Sniffr is not directed at children under 13 and we do not knowingly collect their
          data; email us and we&rsquo;ll delete any such account. (Dogs of all ages are
          welcome.) We protect data with HTTPS/TLS 1.2+ everywhere, hashed passwords
          (bcrypt), short-lived session tokens in secure device storage, encryption at
          rest, and restricted, audited production access. If we ever experience a breach
          affecting your data, we will notify you and the appropriate authorities promptly.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- This site -->
      <section class="mt-16">
        <h2 class="font-display text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight">
          This site
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-[var(--color-muted)] leading-relaxed">
          On sniffrpack.com (run directly by Sniffr) we collect only server logs (IP
          address, user-agent, page requested, retained 30 days for security and traffic
          analysis) and your email address if you fill out a &ldquo;book a setup
          call&rdquo; form. We do not use cookies beyond what is strictly necessary for the
          site to function, and there are no tracking pixels.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Changes / Contact -->
      <section class="mt-16 border-t border-[var(--color-rule)] pt-10">
        <h2 class="font-display text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight">
          Changes &amp; contact
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-[var(--color-muted)] leading-relaxed">
          If we make material changes to this policy, we&rsquo;ll notify you in-app and via
          email before they take effect; the &ldquo;Last updated&rdquo; date above tracks
          the current version. For privacy questions, data access or deletion requests, or
          anything else here, email
          <a href="mailto:joe@sniffrpack.com" class="underline decoration-[var(--color-rule)] hover:text-[var(--color-accent)] hover:decoration-[var(--color-accent)]">joe@sniffrpack.com</a>
          or write to Papyrus Labs, Maplewood, NJ, United States. For questions about how
          your specific data is used or stored, contact your dog walker&rsquo;s business
          first &mdash; they&rsquo;re the controller of that data.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-8 text-sm text-[var(--color-muted)] italic leading-relaxed">
          This is a plain-language privacy policy. We&rsquo;ve tried to be accurate and
          complete rather than legalese-thorough. If something here is unclear or seems to
          contradict what the app actually does, that&rsquo;s a bug &mdash; please tell us
          and we&rsquo;ll fix it.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
